mdl-demo CLI console: you are www-data, in a tmux session that outlives this window.
The Moodle code in demo/ is read-only; extrarepos/ is yours to write in.

Claude Code
  claude-install          install Claude Code, Chromium, Node, Python and diagnostic tools
  claude                  sign in with your own account, then ask for sample data
                          or to reproduce and diagnose a bug
  claude remote-control   drive the session from claude.ai/code or your phone
  Coding agents read AGENTS.md here to learn how to work on this site.

Adding a private plugin
  1. Make a key, and add ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub to the repository as a deploy key:
       ssh-keygen -t ed25519
  2. Clone it into extrarepos/:
       git clone git@github.com:you/moodle-local_example.git extrarepos/example
  3. Install it into the site:
       mdl-repo-add example
  To deploy later changes, commit them in extrarepos/example and run step 3 again.
  Over HTTPS, clone with your username and an access token instead of steps 1 and 2.

Fresh session
  Press Ctrl+D until Reconnect appears at the bottom of this window, then click it.

Copy and paste
  Select with the mouse, Ctrl+C copies, Ctrl+V pastes. Links open on click and the
  wheel scrolls; inside Claude Code, scroll with PgUp and PgDn.

Your Claude login is stored in your home directory, where any PHP on this site can
read it. Run `claude auth logout` before testing untrusted plugins or deleting this demo.
Reset and restore end this session but keep your files. Backups contain only the site,
not your home directory or extrarepos/.

